# The Vercel build is a static preview: the storefront runs on products.json
# and settings.json (checkout hands orders to WhatsApp), and the admin shows
# its sign-in, which says it needs the shop's server. Nothing else runs there.
# Everything below is either server-side, tooling, or documentation, and on a
# static host it would simply be published as readable files. Keeping it out
# of the upload is the difference between shipping a site and shipping the
# source of the server that normally sits behind it.
#
# The real deployment is Railway (Dockerfile + railway.json) and is unaffected
# by this file.

server/
.github/
docs/
*.md
Dockerfile
railway.json
tailwind.*.config.js
tailwind.config.js
tailwind.input.css
tailwind.store.css
eslint.config.js
